    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by the elite 83.29 efficiency score of **Gunnar Henderson**. Facing a 4.32 xERA matchup, **Gunnar Henderson** gains significant leverage from a favorable platoon advantage and his placement in the leadoff spot, making him our cornerstone play. **Drake Baldwin** also emerges as a high-confidence start with a 69.44 score; his 0.377 xwOBA and position atop the lineup against a 4.62 xERA starter in Zac Thornton suggest high run-scoring potential. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.89) and **Kyle Tucker** (63.94) remain locked into the heart of the order, providing the stability necessary to compete in the 5x5 landscape despite facing moderately tough arms.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon advantages to maximize efficiency. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a substantial 14% boost due to dynamic platoon dynamics against Bryce Miller, while **Miguel Vargas** earns his spot at 60.92, bolstered by a 19% SP skill advantage and a slight \"slow delivery\" bonus that favors his base-stealing opportunities. On the bench, **Luis Lara** was the most difficult exclusion; his 51.87 score was hampered primarily by his lower spot in the batting order, which couldn't overcome the efficiency gains seen by our utility options. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that every single lineup slot is currently \"Pending\" official confirmation. **Liam Hicks**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Wade Meckler**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are all currently modeled on projected spots; any late-breaking lineup changes could drastically alter their individual scores. Furthermore, while **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill** possess high-end sprint speed, they face \"Elite Hold\" starting pitchers\u2014a scenario that statistically suppresses our stolen base output. We will monitor these situations closely, as a shift in the opposing defensive battery or a lineup demotion could necessitate a shift toward our bench assets like **Heliot Ramos** or **Jacob Wilson** if their respective roles become more favorable.",
